      ":question/id": "d003578c-c8f1-5f97-8f03-c27729ad3ce6",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-7908",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrices\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}, B = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}, C = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $AB = BA = I_{2}$\n2. $AC = CA = I_{2}$\n3. $B = A^{-1}$"
    },
